<body class="bg-grid scanlines">

  <div class="orb orb-1" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="orb orb-2" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <%- include('partials/header', { currentPage: 'privacy-policy' }) %>

  <main class="journal-wrap" style="padding-top: 6rem;">
    <header class="journal-header reveal">
      <p class="journal-eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="journal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="journal-intro">Last updated: May 30, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div class="journal-divider">&#x2726;</div>

    <article class="chapter reveal">
      <h2 class="chapter-title">1. What data we collect</h2>

      <h3 class="ch-subhead">1.1 Blog accounts (optional)</h3>
      <p>When you register an account on our blog at <code>/blog</code>, we collect:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong> - used for login, never displayed publicly</li>
        <li><strong>Nickname</strong> - shown on your comments and profile</li>
        <li><strong>Password</strong> - stored as a bcrypt hash (never plaintext)</li>
        <li><strong>Comments you post</strong> - publicly visible under your nickname</li>
        <li><strong>Account creation date</strong> - for administrative purposes</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="ch-subhead">1.2 Technical data (automatic)</h3>
      <p>Like any website, our server automatically receives:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>IP address</li>
        <li>Browser type and version</li>
        <li>Operating system</li>
        <li>Referrer URL</li>
        <li>Pages visited and time spent</li>
      </ul>

      <h3 class="ch-subhead">1.3 Cookies</h3>
      <p>We use only one cookie:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Session cookie</strong> (<code>connect.sid</code>) - keeps you logged in for 1 day. No third-party tracking cookies.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <div class="journal-divider">&#x2726;</div>

    <article class="chapter reveal">
      <h2 class="chapter-title">2. What we DON'T collect</h2>
      <p>We do <strong style="color: var(--orange);">not</strong> collect or store:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Real names</li>
        <li>Phone numbers or physical addresses</li>
        <li>Payment information - donations go through Ko-fi, we never see your card details</li>
        <li>We do <strong>not</strong> use Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, or similar trackers</li>
        <li>The entire website source code is <a href="https://github.com/NTNewHorizons/NTNewHorizons.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--orange);">open-source on GitHub</a> - anyone can audit it to verify exactly what data is collected</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <div class="journal-divider">&#x2726;</div>

    <article class="chapter reveal">
      <h2 class="chapter-title">3. How we use your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To let you post comments on the blog</li>
        <li>To protect against spam and abuse</li>
        <li>To troubleshoot technical issues</li>
        <li>We do <strong style="color: var(--orange);">not</strong> sell, rent, or share your data with anyone</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <div class="journal-divider">&#x2726;</div>

    <article class="chapter reveal">
      <h2 class="chapter-title">4. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>Our site uses these external services. Each has its own privacy policy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>YouTube</strong> - embedded video on homepage (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--orange);">Google Privacy Policy</a>)</li>
        <li><strong>Ko-fi</strong> - donation links, payments processed on their servers (<a href="https://ko-fi.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--orange);">Ko-fi Privacy Policy</a>)</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub</strong> - release downloads and API for stats (<a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--orange);">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>)</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> - CDN for Font Awesome icons (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--orange);">Cloudflare Privacy Policy</a>)</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <div class="journal-divider">&#x2726;</div>

    <article class="chapter reveal">
      <h2 class="chapter-title">5. Your rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You can delete your account and all comments via <code>/blog/profile</code></li>
        <li>You can request a copy of all data we hold on you by emailing <strong style="color: var(--orange);">ntnewhorizons@gmail.com</strong></li>
        <li>You can request complete deletion of your data at any time</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <div class="journal-divider">&#x2726;</div>

    <article class="chapter reveal">
      <h2 class="chapter-title">6. Data retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Blog accounts and comments: kept until you delete them or request removal</li>
        <li>Server logs: rotated automatically, maximum retention 30 days</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <div class="journal-divider">&#x2726;</div>

    <article class="chapter reveal">
      <h2 class="chapter-title">7. Contact</h2>
      <p>For privacy questions or data requests:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <strong style="color: var(--orange);">ntnewhorizons@gmail.com</strong></li>
        <li>Discord: <a href="https://discord.gg/wtNVzeE5QB" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--orange);">NT:NH Discord Server</a></li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer', { scripts: ['scripts/about-script.js'] }) %>

</body>
</html>
